{{!-- Where Stonetop's year stands, and what each season does.

      The four seasons are STATED, not merely tinted — the current one is marked with text and with
      aria-current as well as with the band's colour, because colour is never the only carrier of
      anything here.

      The wheel is still a list rather than a row of buttons in the sense that mattered: the year runs
      forwards, and the ONE thing that moves it is the turn control under the box. These buttons never
      set the season. They disclose it — each opens that season's own Seasons Change move, in full,
      below the wheel.

      That replaced a separate "The other seasons" section: three full move rows, numbered by an `ol`
      nobody had written a rule for, spending a screen of height on reference. The wheel already names
      all four and is where a reader looks to ask "what happens in summer?", so the answer is there.
      The current season's move is ALSO the box below, in its steps, and that is fine — a move is not
      a thing the sheet should ration. It renders through the same row in both places, so it rolls,
      posts to chat and reads identically wherever you meet it.

      Params: seasons (SeasonsSnapshot). --}}
<div class="steading-season-head">

	<ol class="steading-wheel" aria-label="{{localize 'stonetop.steading.seasons.wheelLabel'}}">
		{{#each seasons.wheel}}
			<li class="steading-wheel-season{{#if isCurrent}} is-current{{/if}}"
			    {{#if isCurrent}}aria-current="true"{{/if}} data-disclosure-row>
				{{#if move}}
					{{!-- A <button>, not a styled <span>: core binds click only for [data-action], so
					      anything else is keyboard-dead. data-view-state keeps it live on a locked sheet —
					      reading a season's move mutates nothing. --}}
					<button type="button" class="steading-wheel-name" data-action="toggleSeasonMove"
					        data-disclosure data-view-state aria-expanded="false"
					        aria-controls="{{@root.sheetIdPrefix}}-season-{{key}}">{{localize labelKey}}</button>
				{{else}}
					<span class="steading-wheel-name">{{localize labelKey}}</span>
				{{/if}}
			</li>
		{{/each}}
	</ol>

	{{!-- The season in words, with the year — the same fact the ledger line carries, so the tab and
	      the line can never disagree. --}}
	<p class="steading-season-stated">
		{{localize "stonetop.steading.seasons.stated"
		           season=(localize seasons.turnover.season.labelKey) year=seasons.turnover.year}}
	</p>

	{{!-- What the place is like right now, in the book's own words — one line from this steading's
	      own Impressions, stamped when the wheel last turned. Absent for a steadfast that prints no
	      such section, and then the head simply says less. --}}
	{{#if seasons.turnover.impression}}
		<p class="steading-season-impression">{{seasons.turnover.impression}}</p>
	{{/if}}

	{{!-- The disclosed moves, below the wheel rather than inside a segment: a segment is a quarter of
	      a narrow row, and a move does not fit in one. `aria-controls` reaches them from there.

	      `disclosure=false` on the row itself — the wheel segment IS this region's disclosure, and a
	      row that folded again inside it would be two buttons to open one move. A different
	      categoryKey from the turn control's, because the region id is minted from it: the same move
	      drawn twice on one tab must not mint the same id twice. --}}
	{{#each seasons.wheel}}
		{{#if move}}
			<ul class="steading-wheel-move stonetop-unmarked"
			    id="{{@root.sheetIdPrefix}}-season-{{key}}" hidden>
				{{> "stonetop.move-row" move showCheck=false categoryKey="wheel" allowAdditional=false
				    alwaysShowResource=false disclosure=false}}
			</ul>
		{{/if}}
	{{/each}}

</div>
